---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import GamePlayer from '../../components/GamePlayer.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import games from '../../data/games.json';
import skills from '../../data/skills.json';
import { url } from '../../config';

const game = games.find(g => g.id === 'word-building-grade-1')!;
const skill = skills[game.skill as keyof typeof skills];
const page = new URL(url('language-games/word-building-for-grade-1/'), Astro.site).href;
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'LearningResource', name: `${game.keywordTitle}: ${game.title}`,
    url: page, description: game.summary, isAccessibleForFree: true, inLanguage: 'en',
    learningResourceType: 'Educational game', educationalLevel: 'Grade 1', typicalAgeRange: '5-7',
    teaches: 'Blending sounds and spelling short words', timeRequired: 'PT3M', image: new URL(url(game.poster), Astro.site).href,
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: new URL(url(), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Reading games', item: new URL(url('language-games/'), Astro.site).href },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: game.keywordTitle, item: page },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Word Building for Grade 1: Free Spelling Game for Ages 5 to 7 | EduLearnLabs"
  description="A free word building game for Grade 1. Kids hear a word, drag letter tiles to spell it and fill a word wall with 36 picture words. Friendly hints, no ads, no login."
  path="language-games/word-building-for-grade-1/" nav="language" image={game.poster} jsonLd={jsonLd}>

  <Breadcrumbs back={{ name: 'Reading games', path: 'language-games/' }}
    items={[{ name: 'Home', path: '' }, { name: 'Reading games', path: 'language-games/' }, { name: game.keywordTitle, path: 'language-games/word-building-for-grade-1/' }]} />

  <h1>Word Building for Grade 1</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="font-size:20px;max-width:44em">Play <strong>{game.title}</strong>: listen to a word, look at
    its picture and drag letter tiles into place to spell it. Eight words, about 3 minutes, free.</p>

  <GamePlayer game={game} topDifficulty={skill.topDifficulty}
    posterAlt={`${game.title} game screen: a picture card, empty letter slots, a tray of letter tiles and Hazel the owl`} />

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What is Letter Workshop?</h2>
    <p>Letter Workshop is a short spelling game for first graders, set in a cozy craft room where Hazel the owl runs
      the shop. A mouse, hedgehog, bunny or robin comes in holding a picture card, and the voice says the word: "frog".
      Your child drags letter tiles from the tray into the slots on the workbench to build it. Each tile clicks in with
      its own little note, and when the word is done the letters light up one by one, the word is spoken, and a card of
      it goes onto your child's word wall.</p>

    <h2>What kids learn</h2>
    <p>The game practices blending sounds into words and spelling them, a core Grade 1 reading skill. Children hear
      a word, break it into sounds and find the letter for each sound, from left to right. They also match the picture
      to the spoken word, so the word means something. There are 36 picture words in five small steps:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Three letter words like cat, sun and bed</li>
      <li>Three letter words with an extra vowel tile in the tray, so cat and cut are not mixed up</li>
      <li>Missing letters: some tiles are already in place and your child adds the rest</li>
      <li>Four letter words with two consonants together, like frog, drum and star</li>
      <li>Five letter picture words like truck, plant and bread</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <p>Children in Grade 1, usually ages 6 and 7, and Kindergarten children about 5 who already know most letter
      sounds. Every word is spoken aloud and shown as a picture, so early readers can play alone. It works best on a
      tablet, a computer or a phone held sideways.</p>

    <h2>How to play</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Press Play, then tap the big button to start.</li>
      <li>Listen to the word. Tap the picture to hear it again any time.</li>
      <li>Drag a letter tile into a slot. You can also tap a tile and then tap a slot, or type the letter on a keyboard.</li>
      <li>A letter in the wrong place hops back to the tray, ready for another try.</li>
      <li>Not sure? Tap Hazel. She says the word again, shows where the next letter goes, or lights up the letters that
        belong. She never spells the word for you.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Your word wall</h2>
    <p>Every word your child builds becomes a small picture card on their word wall, a shelf of word cards kept on
      this device. Nothing is sent anywhere. A word counts once, the wall never shrinks, and there are no streaks or
      timers, so there is nothing to lose and no pressure to come back.</p>

    <h2>Why it helps</h2>
    <p>Spelling a word by its sounds is the other side of reading it. When a child builds "c, a, t" and hears "cat",
      the link between sounds and letters gets stronger. The game starts easy, steps up after a few words in a row
      and steps back after a couple of tricky ones, so practice stays at the right level. Words your child found hard
      come back next time.</p>

    <h2>Tips for parents</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Play the first game together. Stretch each word as you say it, "fffrrrog", and point left to right.</li>
      <li>Help with letter sounds, not letter names: "c" as in cat, not "see".</li>
      <li>Mixing up b and d is normal at this age. The <a href={url('grown-ups/')}>Grown-ups page</a> shows a simple
        tip when a slip keeps coming back.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">More to play: see all <a href={url('language-games/')}>free reading games</a>, or switch to numbers with
      <a href={url('math-games/addition-for-grade-1/')}>Addition for Grade 1</a> and
      <a href={url('math-games/subtraction-for-grade-1/')}>Subtraction for Grade 1</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <AdSlot id="game-bottom" />
</Base>
